    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d529">

                <pb facs="0468" n="352" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg352"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/986.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Blanchard to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 5, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that the taking
                    of Ouanaminthe has been celebrated in Port au Prince by proclamation, public
                    band concert, night parades arid fireworks, and would be a great step <pb
                        facs="0469" n="353" xml:id="pg353"/> toward pacification were it not for the
                    continued critical financial condition of the Zamor Government.</p>
                <p>The financial condition remains unchanged. The Bank, having already advanced more
                    than 50% of the amount due under the “convention budgétaire,” has declined to
                    advance any more on the August budget. No decision has as yet been reached
                    regarding September advances.</p>
                <p>The question of the issuing of paper money is being contemplated by the
                    Government to enable it to meet its most pressing obligations, payment of
                    troops, etc., as it is without funds whatsoever, and the Bank is now being
                    approached for its support to that end.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. Bailly-Blanchard</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
